  "interpretation": [
    "Four selected joint proposals do not mean four delivery changes: B1C1, B6C1 and B8C2 deliver the same EC/EV task views as dependency composition on those actual parents.",
    "Only B2C2 changes a delivered task view beyond the fixed dependency composition, and only for EV. Its already saved exact-wire audit identifies the retained historical Illinois repair.",
    "This explains why the realized selector has no direct EC-delivery benefit over dependency composition at the measured decisions. It does not prove the final EC ranking against historical task-local controls.",
    "Counterfactual independent policy learning may change parents, teachers, stopping and later proposals; the 13 identical fixed-parent decisions are not an end-to-end equivalence claim.",
    "The full census strengthens the need for the already prepared same-version policy controls. Do not describe all main-versus-control gains as selector gains or rename fixed dependency as the main method."
  ],
  "recomputation_shell_command": ".venv/bin/python -c 'import json,collections; from pathlib import Path; from legal_skill_guard.learning.task_scoped_skills import compose_legal_edits,task_view; from legal_skill_guard.utils.hashing import canonical_json_sha256 as csha\nroot=Path(\"runs/legal_openexempt_native_claim_feedback_public_assets128_20261027_run01\"); bank=[]; out=[]\nfor b in range(1,9):\n pub=json.loads((root/f\"publications/b{b}.json\").read_text()); assert pub[\"parent_bank_sha256\"]==csha(bank)\n for p in sorted((root/\"candidates\").glob(f\"b{b}_candidate*.json\")):\n  d=json.loads(p.read_text()); assert d[\"attempt_parent_bank_sha256\"]==csha(bank)\n  s=d[\"adaptive_commit_selection\"]; a=s[\"component_assessment\"]; dep=bank\n  if a[\"accepted\"]:\n   dep=compose_legal_edits(bank,d[\"proposed_bank\"],d[\"legal_edit_coordinates\"],a[\"accepted_legal_coordinates\"]); assert csha(dep)==a[\"bank_sha256\"]\n  actual=d[\"candidate\"] if d[\"accepted\"] else bank\n  differing=[f for f in (\"EC\",\"EV\") if task_view(actual,f)!=task_view(dep,f)]\n  out.append({\"candidate\":p.name,\"accepted\":d[\"accepted\"],\"selected\":s[\"selected\"],\"joint_admissible\":d[\"proposed_whole_bank_acceptance\"][\"accepted\"],\"dependency_admissible\":a[\"accepted\"],\"joint_gain\":s[\"joint_gain\"],\"dependency_gain\":a[\"gain\"],\"actual_differs_from_fixed_dependency_on_this_parent\":bool(differing),\"differing_tasks\":differing,\"parent_bank_sha256\":csha(bank),\"actual_bank_sha256\":csha(actual),\"dependency_bank_sha256\":csha(dep),\"accepted_dependency_coordinates\":a[\"accepted_legal_coordinates\"]})\n  if d[\"accepted\"]: bank=actual\n assert bank==pub[\"bank\"]\nprint(json.dumps({\"decisions\":len(out),\"counts\":dict(collections.Counter(x[\"selected\"] for x in out)),\"different_from_dependency\":sum(x[\"actual_differs_from_fixed_dependency_on_this_parent\"] for x in out),\"records\":out,\"final_bank_sha256\":csha(bank)},ensure_ascii=False,indent=2))'"
